# Event Record Rules

Every notable event must include city, timestamp, event_type, severity, summary, reason, and reading_id.

The reason field must explain the exact threshold or comparison that caused the event to fire.

Do not create vague event summaries. A reviewer should understand what happened without reading the source code.

Event detection logic should balance sensitivity and noise. Avoid firing repeated events for the same city, timestamp, and event_type.

When adding a new event type, also add a unit test that proves when it should fire and when it should not fire.

Event definitions should be useful to someone monitoring weather across Ottawa, Toronto, and Vancouver, not just technically correct.